From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:03:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Retry HTTP requests when the host name does not resolve

ggl-http retries timeouts and failed connections, but not a host name
that fails to resolve, so one slow answer from the name server fails the
request for good: tesd then has no TES credentials and the deployment
needing them fails. musl's resolver gives up after 5 s, and every request
for credentials or the data plane follows the previous one by longer
than the endpoints' 60 s DNS TTL, so each one asks the network's name
server again. On a board on a home router (one query in 330 took 5 s),
two of three end-to-end test runs failed this way, ~6 s into the
credentials request.

Retry CURLE_COULDNT_RESOLVE_HOST with the same backoff as a failed
connection, and report it as no connection.

Signed-off-by: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Upstream: not yet submitted (developed on the esp32s31/v2.7.0 branch of a fork)
---
 modules/ggl-http/src/gghttp_util.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/ggl-http/src/gghttp_util.c b/modules/ggl-http/src/gghttp_util.c
index 888b4da..30b9e45 100644
--- a/modules/ggl-http/src/gghttp_util.c
+++ b/modules/ggl-http/src/gghttp_util.c
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ static GgError translate_curl_code(CURLcode code) {
     switch (code) {
     case CURLE_OK:
         return GG_ERR_OK;
+    case CURLE_COULDNT_RESOLVE_HOST:
     case CURLE_COULDNT_CONNECT:
     case CURLE_NO_CONNECTION_AVAILABLE:
     case CURLE_RECV_ERROR:
@@ -79,6 +80,9 @@ static bool can_retry(CURLcode code, CurlData *data) {
         break;
 
     case CURLE_OPERATION_TIMEDOUT:
+    // A name server that does not answer in time (musl gives up after
+    // 5 s) is as transient as a connection that fails.
+    case CURLE_COULDNT_RESOLVE_HOST:
     case CURLE_COULDNT_CONNECT:
     case CURLE_SSL_CONNECT_ERROR:
     case CURLE_GOT_NOTHING:
